'' A CAST TO A POINTER OVER A UDT WITH NO POINTER 'operator cast' is fbc's error 28 -- measured on
'' fbc-modern 1.20, lines 55 to 65: a type casting to string, to long or to integer, one with only
'' a constructor, and one whose pointer cast is in its BASE. Such a UDT "may convert", so nothing
'' judged it, Check left the cast untyped and the statement stopped on TKO0994.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/cast-udt-no-ptr-cast.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
